# The locus units that should be ON. deploy/server-sync.sh enables every unit listed here and
# disables (stops) any enabled locus unit that is not, so switching a timer on or off is a commit,
# never a hand step on the server. Oneshot services fired by a timer are not listed: they have no
# [Install] section and are started by their timer. One unit per line; `#` starts a comment.
locus-backup.timer
locus-capture.timer
locus-watch.timer
# Removed with their code in Slice C (C2): discover-pull, maintain, daily, daily-pull,
# discover-harvest and remarkable-receiver. server-sync.sh deletes their unit files.
# The calendar daemon (kairos, ADR-008): restarted only when its build ran, not on every deploy.
locus-kairosd.service
# The HTTP service (Slice 0.6): MCP for every Claude, one process.
locus-http.service
# heuris (H1): mail, calendar, chats and repos indexed into heuris.db every 15 minutes.
locus-heuris.timer
# heuris (H2): facts from mail and the calendar, records and briefs, hourly on the API credit.
locus-heuris-derive.timer
# The public listener (H1.10): claude.ai and the phone, OAuth with a passphrase, via Funnel.
locus-public.service
